    P("The label hierarchy has the larger effect because it removes distinctions that composition supports only weakly. On unseen sources the three broad groups are recognised with 89% balanced accuracy, six points below the random-split value, against a loss of nineteen points for the eight settings. What transfers between sources is thus mainly the first-order contrast between arc, ridge and intraplate magmas, and what fails to transfer is mainly the finer division within these groups. We suggest only that a prediction be reported as a broad group with the candidate settings within it, in place of a single eight-way label.")
    P("The ternary diagram makes a related point with two ratios. A linear rule in ln(Nb/La) and ln(La/Yb) has six coefficients and cannot adapt to individual suites, so it loses little on unseen sources. Nb/La is low in subduction-related magmas, and also in magmas contaminated by continental crust or lithosphere; La/Yb rises with source enrichment, with decreasing degree of melting and with residual garnet. The search arrived at the elements of the La–Y–Nb diagram of Cabanis and Lecolle (1989), with Yb in place of Y, and at a similar accuracy; our contribution is a boundary fitted to a large compilation and an estimate of its error on unseen sources, not a better choice of elements. The diagram is valid for oceanic arc, ridge and ocean-island basalts only, its third field also receives enriched ridge basalts, La is less immobile than the high-field-strength elements, and LightGBM is 8.5 points more accurate on the same samples. It may serve where only a few elements are available.")
    Aa({'type': 'h2', 'text': '5.4. Recommendations'})
    P("Models intended for new samples should be validated with whole sources, preferably whole localities, held out, with feature selection and scaling fitted inside the training folds and with intervals from a bootstrap over sources. Compilations should be screened for samples that appear under more than one code or database. Class-wise recall should accompany overall accuracy, predictions are better reported hierarchically, and predicted probabilities should be checked on held-out sources. Diagrams derived from data should be selected and assessed in nested steps and compared with a multivariate model on the same samples.")
    Aa({'type': 'h2', 'text': '5.5. Limitations'})
